/* basic.c - P8X BASIC written in C (2026-09-13), the size/speed twin of the
 * hand-assembled basic/p8xbasic.asm. Same language, tokens (the .BAS format),
 * messages, prompts, limits and GL byte streams; the twelve BASIC tests run
 * against either build. TPA build only (RUN /binc/basic.bin under the OS; BYE
 * returns to the shell).
 *
 * Build:  cat basic/glkwtab.c basic/basic.c > basicc.c  (the GL verb tables,
 *         generated by generators/gen_glkw.py)  ->  clib.py -> p8cc.py
 * Layout: code at $5900; the interpreter's big tables are raw memory above the
 * image ($C600 variables, $C700 string work buffers, $C800 string variables,
 * $CA80 program, $E000 rebuild scratch). The asm twin keeps the equivalent
 * tables at its own BASRAM=$8000 base ($8100 variables, $8300 string variables,
 * $8580 program, PBUF $E000 in the TPA build), so the two binaries are both
 * code + small data and the comparison is like for like.
 *
 * Subset notes: int is 16-bit and compares/divides UNSIGNED, so a signed BASIC
 * compare flips the sign bit of both sides first (sgn()); there is no longjmp,
 * so an error sets `err` and every parse level returns through it.
 */
